{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural next choice after Old Sock and Memphis because I want relaxed blues-rock with familiar, song-focused material.",
    "Croz and Le Noise connect with the songwriting I enjoyed around You Should Be So Lucky, even though I would save them for a different mood."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Endless River's atmospheric instrumental focus and Homo Erraticus's progressive concept feel distant from the blues and roots-rock songs I want now.",
    "Carry On and Wings Over America involve lengthy retrospective or live listening, while Muddy Wolf at Red Rocks has fitting blues material but not the studio setting I would choose today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat familiar classic-rock artists as equally relevant, although their albums can offer very different listening experiences.",
    "Shared rock roots seem to count too heavily when early acoustic demos, instrumental music, and progressive concepts do not satisfy my current mood."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My interest in Old Sock and Memphis points toward relaxed blues and roots-rock, which explains why The Breeze stands out more than the other choices.",
    "An artist or sound can interest me without making an album something I would choose now; today I prefer a studio album over a long live set or retrospective."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my broad rock interests but only partly capture my current preference for relaxed, song-focused blues and roots-rock studio albums."
}"}
